
val name: String? = "Peter"
name?.let { safeName ->
    // This code block ONLY runs if name is not null.
    // 'safeName' is the non-nullable version of 'name'.
    println("The name is $safeName")
    println("Length is ${safeName.length}")
}
   Here is what happens: 1.      name?. performs a safe call. If name is null, nothing after it happens. The whole block is skipped. 
2.      If name is NOT null, the let block is executed. 3.    
Inside the block, we have access to the value. By default, it is named it, but we can rename it (like safeName) to be clearer.
